# The story with the decode's per-token code in internal RAM (the backend's
# CONFIG_ESP32_BACKEND_HOT_IRAM: ESP32_HOT_CODE functions, the PIE kernels and
# ExecuTorch's instruction loop), for a board A/B against the plain build:
#   run_story_hardware.py --reuse-artifact --sdkconfig-extra sdkconfig.hotiram.defaults ...
# builds it in build_story_hw_hotiram. The internal heap shrinks by what
# .iram0.text grows; compare the boot's "[mem]" line and the KV cache's
# "shared mem-id-2 ... (internal)" before comparing ms/token. The 27 KB come
# from what the story's floor lets it place after load: decode's own
# activations (33.8 KB, on by default) do not fit beside it, so the
# placement alternative is this file with --no-decode-act-internal.
CONFIG_ESP32_BACKEND_HOT_IRAM=y
